\section*{A size-independent Gibbs Poincaré constant throughout high-temperature SK}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents a proof in the selected manuscript. Throughout fixed SK temperatures $0<\beta<1$, the rate-one heat-bath gap is claimed bounded below by a positive constant with high disorder probability.

\subsection{Mathematical statement of the claimed result}
\paragraph{Result 1.} For independent standard Gaussian $J_{ij}$, $i<j$, with $J_{ji}=J_{ij},J_{ii}=0$, use the zero-field SK measure
\[
 \pi_{n,\beta}^J(x)=Z^{-1}\exp\left(\frac\beta{\sqrt n}\sum_{i<j}J_{ij}x_ix_j\right),\qquad x\in\{-1,1\}^n.
\]
Continuous heat-bath dynamics refreshes every site at rate one; a discrete step refreshes one uniformly selected site, including attempts that retain its spin. For fixed $0<\beta<1$, a finite deterministic $C_\beta$ satisfies
\[
 \mathbb P_J\left\{\operatorname{Var}_\pi(f)\le C_\beta\sum_{i=1}^n
 \mathbb E_\pi(f-\mathbb E_\pi[f\mid x_{-i}])^2
 \text{ for all }f:\{-1,1\}^n\to\mathbb R\right\}\longrightarrow1.
\]
The continuous-time spectral gap is at least $C_\beta^{-1}$ on this event; the uniform-site discrete gap is at least $(nC_\beta)^{-1}$. This theorem uses zero external field.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Gaussian-observation stochastic localization transports a functional inequality from posterior systems. Stopped entropy estimates control rare observation paths weighted by a test function, and stable-field plus random-matrix estimates retain enough variance to obtain a dimension-free Poincare bound.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
Throughout fixed SK temperatures $0<\beta<1$, the rate-one heat-bath gap is claimed bounded below by a positive constant with high disorder probability. The question retains these same parameters and conventions. Within these assumptions, this is a claimed affirmative answer to the stated question.

\subsection{Formal verification}
For family 227, the selected statements include the high-temperature gap for $\beta<1$, cutoff ratios only for $\beta<1/2$, critical lower mixing scales with a subexponential upper bound, and low-temperature barriers. They do not provide the full critical exponent, the full cutoff location, or the newer autocorrelation limits. The listed Comparator files are \texttt{CriticalSK.lean}, \texttt{CriticalSKMixing.lean}, \texttt{SKBarriers.lean}, \texttt{SKHighTemperature.lean}, \texttt{SKRatio.lean}. Named declarations include \texttt{OAI.CriticalSK.covariance\_and\_linear\_tests}, \texttt{OAI.CriticalSK.critical\_mixing\_bounds}. This site has not executed the Lean code. The scope descriptions do not certify the remaining manuscript arguments.

\subsection{Status caveat}
OpenAI attributes these manuscripts to work by an internal model. Its release cautions that arguments without formalization can contain mistakes. This catalogue has not independently checked the proofs; the labels report the mathematical claims attributed to OpenAI.

